WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.554
<v Human Services Manager>Thanks for the email about evening callers. That data is

00:00:03.554 --> 00:00:07.108
<v Human Services Manager>exactly what the schedule needs. I am curious, though. Why

00:00:07.108 --> 00:00:09.240
<v Human Services Manager>not raise it in the meeting?

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:12.710
<v Call-Line Worker>Honestly? The county directors and providers were going back and

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.830
<v Call-Line Worker>forth. I am the newest person on the team. It

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.702
<v Call-Line Worker>did not feel like my place.

00:00:18.052 --> 00:00:21.494
<v Human Services Manager>That is fair, and it is common. In one study,

00:00:21.494 --> 00:00:24.937
<v Human Services Manager>34 of 40 employees said they had held back on

00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:28.380
<v Human Services Manager>an important issue. Lack of rank was one of the

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.068
<v Human Services Manager>top reasons.

00:00:29.418 --> 00:00:32.704
<v Call-Line Worker>There was also a feeling it would not matter. The

00:00:32.704 --> 00:00:35.990
<v Call-Line Worker>invitation said everything was open, but then the venue turned

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.962
<v Call-Line Worker>out to be fixed. People noticed.

00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:41.316
<v Human Services Manager>That one is on me. I should have corrected the

00:00:41.316 --> 00:00:44.320
<v Human Services Manager>invitation before the meeting. Saying what is fixed and what

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.324
<v Human Services Manager>is open is the least I owe people who show

00:00:47.324 --> 00:00:47.624
<v Human Services Manager>up.

00:00:47.974 --> 00:00:50.518
<v Call-Line Worker>Would it have changed anything if I had spoken up?

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:54.502
<v Human Services Manager>Yes. The two extra hours are still open. Your data

00:00:54.502 --> 00:00:58.137
<v Human Services Manager>points to a weekday evening. That is a real choice,

00:00:58.137 --> 00:01:01.044
<v Human Services Manager>and the decision is not until next week.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.266
<v Call-Line Worker>So what do you want me to do?

00:01:03.616 --> 00:01:06.565
<v Human Services Manager>Share the weeks and times directly with the decision group.

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:09.515
<v Human Services Manager>And next meeting, I will run rounds and start with

00:01:09.515 --> 00:01:12.464
<v Human Services Manager>people who hold the least rank. That way it is

00:01:12.464 --> 00:01:14.824
<v Human Services Manager>not on you to fight for a turn.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:18.076
<v Call-Line Worker>That would help. Will people hear what happened with their

00:01:18.076 --> 00:01:18.366
<v Call-Line Worker>input?

00:01:18.716 --> 00:01:22.340
<v Human Services Manager>They will. The report-back will say what was considered, what

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.964
<v Human Services Manager>changed, what did not and why. If your evening hour

00:01:25.964 --> 00:01:29.588
<v Human Services Manager>gets adopted, it will say your data is the reason.

00:01:29.938 --> 00:01:32.620
<v Call-Line Worker>Then I will speak up next time. Mostly because I

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.498
<v Call-Line Worker>will know it can still change something.
